# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Kamal Singh Nayal et al. (2026). Critical benchmarking of machine-learned interatomic potentials for intermolecular and noncovalent interactions.
#   Machine Learning Science and Technology. doi:10.1088/2632-2153/aea39f
#
# Version read: publisher (sha256 b43573c1fe4ad894...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 238 (Dataset/benchmark). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/nayal2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the five MLIPs of Table 3 (AIMNet2(2023) B97-3c,
# AIMNet2(2025) trained here by continual pretraining, MACE-OFF23(M),
# MACE-OMol, UMA-S-OMol) with their R2, RMSE and MAE of interaction
# energies against CCSD(T)/CBS references on 21 benchmark data sets (with
# element/charge-compatible subsets marked as separate rows). The other
# AIMNet2 and MACE-OFF variants (SI), overlap analysis and dimer curves
# are not encoded.

