###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# AIMNet2(2025) was trained on a single H200 GPU for about 4 million steps
# (Sec. 2.1.3). No inference timing is tabulated.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Errors are on interaction (binding) energies of dimers and complexes in kcal/mol; S12L uses back-corrected experimental binding energies flagged as possibly unreliable. Rows marked with a superscript in Table 3 are model-compatible subsets; here '-a' rows are the AIMNet2/MACE-OMol/UMA subset and '-b' rows the MACE-OFF subset.
# - UMA-S-OMol is recorded under the new registry method UMA (the paper says UMA 'builds upon eSEN'; no derivation edge since UMA's introducing paper is not in the corpus). MACE-OFF23(M) and MACE-OMol have no registry model rows.
# - The L7 row of Table 3 is split across lines in the text layer; its R2 values (-1.86, -1.20) were matched to the AIMNet2 columns by position. Worth a check.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/nayal2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

